/target

# Web UI: node deps are installed per-checkout; the built SPA (web/dist) IS
# committed so `cargo install --git` embeds it without needing Node.
/web/node_modules

# Editor swap files
*.swp

# Personal scratch notes
/TODO.md

# Generated by the e2e tests (tests/cli.rs) — all except the three that the *unit* tests
# in `src/` also read. Those are committed, because a test binary must not depend on
# another test binary having run first: `cargo test` runs the bin's unit tests before the
# integration tests that write these, so on a clean checkout every consumer failed with
# "no such file". They are ~2 KB of tensor data built from byte ramps — a cheap price for
# deleting an ordering dependency between test binaries. `write_fixture` still rewrites
# them on each run, and the bytes can differ: the metadata is a `HashMap`, whose iteration
# order Rust randomises per process, so the `__metadata__` JSON keys come out in a
# different order. Same keys, same length, same meaning — every consumer parses the JSON —
# so a local test run may show these two as modified. That churn is noise; don't commit it.
/tests/fixtures/*.safetensors
!/tests/fixtures/tiny.safetensors
!/tests/fixtures/diff_old.safetensors
!/tests/fixtures/diff_new.safetensors
/tests/fixtures_moe/

# Python bytecode from the compileall syntax gate
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# Review notes dropped in the tree while working — like TODO.md, they are not the deliverable.
/CODE_REVIEW.md
/ARCHITECTURE_REVIEW.md
/WEB_DIFF_UX_REVIEW.md

# Throwaway Playwright checks written while verifying a change in a real browser.
web/qa-*.mjs
